# LF in the repository and in every working copy, on every platform, whatever `core.autocrlf`
# says. Several tests read source files and match them with patterns written for LF (for example
# `tests/readonly-guard.test.ts`), so a CRLF checkout — Git for Windows' default — fails them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# IFC-SPF (ISO 10303-21) is a text format. The two committed fixtures are generated text
# (`scripts/make-tiny-ifc.py`), the tests read them as UTF-8, and the parser takes either line
# ending; LF everywhere means a fixture is the same bytes, and the same SHA-256, on every OS.
*.ifc text eol=lf

# The binary types the repository holds: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.bmp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff2 binary
